---
title: Results survive compute termination
---
sequenceDiagram
  accTitle: PodVigil result delivery
  accDescr: The supervisor stops workload writers and snapshots outputs to persistent storage. Pod deletion and verified absence come before S3 retrieval. Only a verified local backup and whole-volume audit authorize deletion of the owned volume. Incomplete recovery retains storage and reports ongoing billing risk.

  participant POD as Pod supervisor
  participant VOL as Owned volume
  participant API as Runpod API
  participant CTRL as Controller or watchdog
  participant BACK as Local backup

  POD->>POD: Stop workload writers
  POD->>VOL: Snapshot outputs and manifest
  POD->>API: Attempt own-Pod DELETE
  CTRL->>API: Verify compute absence
  Note over API,CTRL: Accepted DELETE alone is not proof

  CTRL->>VOL: Retrieve bytes through S3
  VOL-->>BACK: Save artifacts and control records
  CTRL->>BACK: Verify sizes and SHA-256
  CTRL->>VOL: Audit the whole volume

  alt All objects covered and unchanged
    CTRL->>API: Delete owned volume
    CTRL->>API: Verify volume absence
    CTRL-->>BACK: Record complete backup and cleanup
  else Missing, changed or unknown objects
    CTRL-->>BACK: Preserve available outputs and recovery evidence
    Note over VOL,BACK: Volume retained, storage may still bill
  end
